								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:30:00.156946+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:30:00.156946+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "EE2FcPzaSemyYF+WBA3wkQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Each stored report is one folder `<type>/<yyyy-mm-dd>/<storage id>/` ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#folderFor:storageId:machineName:|label=#selector}} in {{gtClass:GtReportsStore}}). The storage id is the UTC time plus a short random part, for example `20261108T093015Z-c8538f0a` ({{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#newStorageId|label=#selector}}); the date folder is its UTC day. Files are named after the report type ({{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#reportType|label=#selector}}), e.g. `message-tally.txt` and `message-tally.json`, or after their role when a report has several files of the same kind (`picture-1.png`, `picture-2.png`, written with {{gtMethod:GtReportsStoreEntry>>#writeBytes:named:extension:|label=#selector}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:30:00.156948+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-10T13:30:00.156948+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "G/75YvvrQsKUUdpk2TsqpA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "`meta.json` ({{gtClass:GtReportMetadata}}) is written last, so a folder without it is incomplete. It holds three names: the report type ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#reportType|label=#selector}}: the kind of data, used for the folders and for grouping), the report class ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#reportClassName|label=#selector}}: how to read the report now) and the report alias ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#reportAlias|label=#selector}}: how to read it after a class rename). It holds two ids: the report uid ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#reportUid|label=#selector}}), given to the report when it is created ({{gtMethod:GtProcessesReport>>#initialize|label=#selector}}), and the storage id of this copy ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#storageId|label=#selector}}). Storing the same report again gives a new storage id but the same report uid, so copies can be recognised. `meta.json` also holds the UTC time, the image data, the data files with their sizes ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata>>#files|label=#selector}}, {{gtClass:GtReportFileDescription}}), the format version ({{gtMethod:GtReportMetadata class>>#currentFormatVersion|label=#selector}}) and a machine name, empty in plain GT ({{gtMethod:GtReportImageData>>#machineName|label=#selector}}, {{gtMethod:GtReportsStore>>#machineNameFor:|label=#selector}})."
						}
					]
				},
